s6-rc service source tree
=========================

Services live in numbered phase folders. The number is a HUMAN MAP of the boot
phase, grouped by function and assigned in tens so there is room to insert:

    10-base       device nodes + storage foundation (mdev, mounts, hwclock)
    20-logging    syslogd, klogd
    30-network    wifi bring-up chain (brcmfmac -> wpa_supplicant -> dhcpcd ...)
    40-usb        usb0 gadget net (setup-usb0, udhcpd-usb0)
    50-services   general daemons (crond, ntpd, watchdog, dropbear, getty)
    60-app        shareframe-application, shareframe-dashboard
    90-health     rauc-mark-good
    bundles       the 'default' bundle brought up at boot

IMPORTANT — the number does NOT control run order
--------------------------------------------------
s6-rc derives startup order entirely from each service's `dependencies` file.
Thus the dependency graph is the source of truth.
